461	    /**
462	     * The {@code membershipLevel} reported for a single owner. Starts from the owner-local derivation
463	     * in {@link OwnerMapper#membershipLevel(Owner)} (the level from the owner's own membership points),
464	     * routed through the controller so the create audit log and the single-owner response agree on one
465	     * value. Unlike the mapper - which sees only the owner - the controller can reach the rest of the
466	     * clinic, so this is the single place a reported membership level is shaped by cross-owner context.
467	     *
468	     * <p>Household ceiling: the reported level is capped at one above the current maximum
469	     * {@linkplain #householdMemberLevel(Owner) level} among the owner's <em>existing</em>
470	     * {@link #householdMembers(Owner) household members} (those sharing its {@code householdId}, other
471	     * than the owner itself). With no existing household member no cap applies and the owner-local level
472	     * is reported unchanged. The cap uses each member's own owner-local level (not their reported,
473	     * capped level), so it depends only on the members' own points and cannot recurse.
474	     *
475	     * @param owner the owner whose reported membership level is wanted
476	     * @return the owner's membership level, capped at one above its household maximum
477	     */
478	    private Integer membershipLevel(Owner owner) {
479	        int ownLevel = ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner);
480	        java.util.OptionalInt maxHouseholdLevel = householdMembers(owner).stream()
481	            .filter(member -> !java.util.Objects.equals(member.getId(), owner.getId()))
482	            .mapToInt(this::householdMemberLevel)
483	            .max();
484	        if (maxHouseholdLevel.isEmpty()) {
485	            return ownLevel;
486	        }
487	        return Math.min(ownLevel, maxHouseholdLevel.getAsInt() + 1);
488	    }
489	
490	    /**
491	     * The owner-local membership level of a household member, used only as an input to the household
492	     * ceiling in {@link #membershipLevel(Owner)}. The member's {@link Owner#getHouseholdSize()
493	     * household size} is set from its household before the level is derived, so the member's household
494	     * factor is accounted for exactly as it is when the member is reported on its own; the level itself
495	     * comes from the owner-local {@link OwnerMapper#membershipLevel(Owner)}.
496	     *
497	     * @param member an existing member of an owner's household
498	     * @return the member's owner-local membership level
499	     */

